  "result": "I found the cause and wrote a plan, but I haven't changed any code because plan mode is active. I couldn't call ExitPlanMode here, so please approve the plan or tell me to proceed.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py:603-635` uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment start by default. As a result, `cli a#b c` is split into `[\"cli\", \"a\"]`, and `cli #x y` loses everything after `cli`. Bash, Zsh, Fish and PowerShell completion all go through this function, so all four are affected. I found this by reading the source and `shlex`'s documented behaviour, and I haven't run the code.\n\n**Fix:** After `lex.whitespace_split = True` at line 624, add `lex.commenters = \"\"`. I'd also add a `CHANGES.md` entry.\n\n**Tests:** I'd add `#` cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`. I'd also add an end-to-end case to `test_full_complete` in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`.\n\n**Verification:** Run `pytest tests/test_parser.py tests/test_shell_completion.py tests/test_deprecations.py`. The new cases should fail before the change and pass after it.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-foamy-nova.md`.",
